  "texts": {
    "preamble": "The State Of Maharashtra vs Shantaram Narayan Chile on 6 January, 2016 919 Apeal 813 Of 2002.doc vks In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Criminal Appeal No.813 Of 2002 State of Maharashtra ] at the instance of ] Shri. S. H. Joshi, ] Food Inspector, ] Appellant Office of Assistant Commissioner ] Original Food and Drug Administration (M.S.) ] Complainant. Dr. Babasaheb Ambedkar Roadig ]",
    "facts": "2. Brief facts of the appeal can be stated as follows :- On 13th September, 1995 at about 8.30 a.m., P.W.1 Food Inspector Shri. S. H. Joshi, intervened the respondent and enquired with him about the contents in the cans which he was carrying. Respondent disclosed that the cans contain buffalo milk and he was carrying the same for selling it to the customers. P.W.1 Food Inspector Joshi, disclosed his identity and intimated respondent his intention of drawing sample of said milk for the purpose of analysis. P.W.1 Food Inspector Joshi, then purchased 750 milliliter of buffalo milk from the can for Rs.6/- and divided it, into three bottles of equal quantity. He added 20 drops formalin in each bottle as preservative of milk. The bottles were corked tightly and sealed in the presence of panchas. Then requisite formalities of issuing notices in form VI and under Section 14(a) of the Act, were completed. One of 919 APEAL 813 OF 2002.doc the sample bottles, was sent to Local Heal Authority; whereas one was sent to Public Analyst. The report of Public Analyst, disclosed that the sample was not conforming to the standard of buffalo milk, as laid down in the Rules under Prevention of Food Adulteration Act. Hence all the papers were sent to the Joint Commissioner, Konkan Division, Food and Drug Administration on 26.10.1995, for necessary sanction. On receipt of the sanction, P.W.1 Food Inspector Shri. Joshi, filed private criminal case against respondent, for the various offences, as noted above, for selling adulterated buffalo milk and selling it The State Of Maharashtra vs Shantaram Narayan Chile on 6 January, 2016 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/134760377/ 2 without having any licence. 3. On the receipt of summons, respondent appeared and pleaded not guilty. In the trial Court, P.W.1 examined himself and two panchas viz P.W.2 Babaji Arekar, P.W.3 Gopal Bhat. Both of them did not support the case. Prosecution also led evidence of Senior Clerk of Local Health Authority P.W.4 Shrinivas Kulkarni and then closed its case. 919 APEAL 813 OF 2002.doc 5.",
